{%- doc -%}
  @param {number} rating - The review's star rating, 1-5.
  @param {string} quote - The review text.
  @param {string} name - The reviewer's display name.
  @param {number} card_index - This card's 0-based position among the rendered cards. Used only to
    build a unique accessible name when the reviewer's name is hidden.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- comment -%}
  One Google review card, as a configurable block.

  sections/mionas-google-reviews.liquid renders this once per selected review, as a *static* block
  with a fixed id inside its for-loop -- the same shape sections/product-list.liquid uses for
  blocks/_product-card.liquid, and what Horizon's "Featured collection" sections do. A static block
  may be rendered in a loop, and because every iteration shares one id, the theme editor shows a
  single card block whose settings govern every card. That is the correct shape here: which reviews
  appear rotates daily, so there is no stable per-card thing to configure.

  Data arrives as arbitrary parameters on the content_for tag (rating/quote/name), not as
  closest.metaobject.google_review. Both are supported, but the section already loops
  metaobjects.google_review.values and owns the enabled/rotation logic, so it necessarily knows the
  field names -- passing them keeps the metaobject schema in one file and leaves this block a pure
  presentation layer. If merchants ever need to bind other review fields through the theme editor's
  dynamic-sources picker, closest.metaobject.google_review is the route to switch to.

  Private (`_`-prefixed) because it renders nothing on its own: without the parameters the section
  passes, it is an empty card.

  The markup comes from snippets/mionas-google-review-card.liquid, the same snippet
  blocks/mionas-review-card.liquid renders from hand-entered settings, so a Google review and a
  hand-entered testimonial stay one component with different data behind them. This file adds no
  markup and no CSS of its own -- only the three merchant choices, plus the
  accessible name the snippet gives the "Leer más" trigger and its dialog.

  quote_clamp_lines replaced an earlier quote_max_characters setting that truncated in Liquid.
  Truncation is destructive -- the cut text never reached the DOM -- so it could not coexist with
  a control that reveals the rest. Clamping by lines also evens out card heights, which a
  character count cannot: wrapping and font metrics vary.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% liquid
  # A hidden author is passed as blank rather than suppressed inside the snippet: the snippet
  # already treats a blank name as "no attribution", so no extra parameter is needed for it.
  assign card_name = ''
  if block.settings.show_author
    assign card_name = name
  endif

  # A unique, human-meaningful accessible name per card -- six cards must not all announce a bare
  # "Leer más". The name is the useful identifier when it is shown; the position is the only thing
  # left when it is not.
  if card_name != blank
    assign card_dialog_label = 'Reseña de ' | append: card_name
  else
    assign card_position = card_index | plus: 1
    assign card_dialog_label = 'Reseña ' | append: card_position
  endif
%}

{%- comment -%}
  Loaded here rather than in snippets/scripts.liquid so the cost lands only on pages that render
  a Google review. The block renders once per card, so these tags repeat -- browsers dedupe
  identical module URLs, and blocks/popup-link.liquid loads dialog.js the same way.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'dialog.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>
<script src="{{ 'mionas-review-clamp.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>

{% render 'mionas-google-review-card',
  rating: rating,
  show_rating: block.settings.show_rating,
  quote: quote,
  name: card_name,
  clamp_lines: block.settings.quote_clamp_lines,
  dialog_label: card_dialog_label,
  shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes
%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Mionas: Google review",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_rating",
      "label": "Show star rating",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_author",
      "label": "Show reviewer name",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "quote_clamp_lines",
      "label": "Collapsed height",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 10,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 5,
      "unit": "ln",
      "info": "0 shows the full review. Any other value collapses longer reviews to that many lines and adds a 'Leer más' link that opens the full text."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
